 * Isolates the cache-assembler/ejector. One variable: the weights on the signals
 * the eviction score combines. Everything upstream held fixed (units = turns,
 * fingerprints deterministic). OFFLINE, no model — keep-needed recall is a
 * fingerprint fact, so every (turn × past-unit) pair is a datapoint (high power).
 *
 * THE NON-DEGENERACY RULE (why this measures anything): the assembler evicts at
 * t−1 using ONLY turns 0..t−1, to prepare for turn t which it cannot see. So
 * "relevance" is to the RECENT window, and "needed" is the FUTURE turn t. A unit
 * dormant in the recent window but referenced again at t (non-monotonic return,
 * H1) is the case that decides the weights — recency/recent-relevance drop it,
 * PRIORITY keeps it.
