 *
 * GROUND TRUTH: needed(u,t) = fingerprint(u) ∩ fingerprint(t) ≠ ∅ (referenced at t);
 *   horizon variant: referenced within [t, t+H).
 * METRIC: keep-needed recall @ budget M (task-critical), and separately on the
 *   NON-MONOTONIC subset (needed AND dormant > D turns). Occupancy = M (token proxy).
 *   Asymmetric by the operator's rule: dropping-needed is the failure; keeping-extra is cheap.
 *
 * PRE-REGISTERED: a signal EARNS its weight iff adding it lifts keep-needed recall
 *   (esp. non-monotonic) over the recency-only baseline by >=0.03 at equal M.
 *
 * RERUN: node experiments/assembler-weighting/assembler-weighting.mjs [--session 2]
 * ============================================================================
